<!-- @en -->
Deploy your application to Netlify. You'll need a hosted database backend (we recommend PocketHost) and configured Netlify environment variables.

New projects build with `@sveltejs/adapter-node`, which is what [`vela deploy`](/deploy) runs. Switch to Netlify's adapter first:

```
$ npm uninstall @sveltejs/adapter-node
$ npm install -D @sveltejs/adapter-netlify
```

Then import the adapter from `@sveltejs/adapter-netlify` in `vite.config.ts`:

```ts
import adapter from '@sveltejs/adapter-netlify';
```

Set the environment variables and deploy:

```
$ netlify env:set POCKETBASE_URL
$ netlify env:set POCKETBASE_SUPERUSER_EMAIL
$ netlify env:set POCKETBASE_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD
$ netlify deploy
```
<!-- @es -->
Despliega tu aplicación en Netlify. Necesitarás un backend de base de datos alojada (recomendamos PocketHost) y variables de entorno de Netlify configuradas.

Los proyectos nuevos se compilan con `@sveltejs/adapter-node`, que es lo que ejecuta [`vela deploy`](/es/deploy). Cambia primero al adaptador de Netlify:

```
$ npm uninstall @sveltejs/adapter-node
$ npm install -D @sveltejs/adapter-netlify
```

Después importa el adaptador desde `@sveltejs/adapter-netlify` en `vite.config.ts`:

```ts
import adapter from '@sveltejs/adapter-netlify';
```

Configura las variables de entorno y despliega:

```
$ netlify env:set POCKETBASE_URL
$ netlify env:set POCKETBASE_SUPERUSER_EMAIL
$ netlify env:set POCKETBASE_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD
$ netlify deploy
```
<!-- @end -->
